<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Otho de la Roche</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1234</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Othon de la Roche</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otho">Otho</a> de la <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hoffmann-la-roche">Roche</a> was a Burgundian knight of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fourth-crusade">Fourth Crusade</a> who received <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> and Thebes from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boniface-i-marquis-of-montferrat">Boniface of Montferrat</a> in 1205 and became the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> lord of Athens. He also held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argo">Argos</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nafplio">Nauplia</a> as a fief of the Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaea">Achaea</a>. Around 1225 he returned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a>, leaving his Greek lands to his nephew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guy-i-de-la-roche">Guy I de la Roche</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/otho-de-la-roche.jpg" alt="Otho de la Roche" width="320" height="268" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original design: unknown 13th-century artist; Sketch: Gustave Schlumberger (1844–1929) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seal_of_Othon_de_la_Roche_(Schlumberger,_1897).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
